  {
   "id": "MmhQpgR5IDkJ",
   "from": "Ben Goodrich",
   "author": "743bbacc59f4b25f",
   "date": "2012-12-20T09:15:04Z",
   "subject": "Re: stan runtime error \"Exception: boost::too_many_args: format-string referred...\"",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "On Wednesday, December 19, 2012 10:06:42 PM UTC-5, Will Morris wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">Could someone please help me out with this runtime error (below) I am getting. Have tried to run this model (<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px\"><a href=\"http://cl.ly/131S3n330Z1K\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://cl.ly/131S3n330Z1K&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468625307000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1-gRbjuGJB_HvTCeKYscRy\">http://cl.ly/131S3n330Z1K</a></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px\">, with data </span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px\"><a href=\"http://cl.ly/code/0G3z0o441S0E\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://cl.ly/code/0G3z0o441S0E&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468625307000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0tMiS7xNSdUKOQ4P9KoEsf\">http://cl.ly/code/0G3z0o441S0E</a></span>)\r\n on both a Mac and Linux with optimisation on and off. Both give this \r\nerror I can&#39;t interpret. Stan (v-1.1.0) itself is working fine as I can \r\nrun the example models without error.</blockquote>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div><br>This is our bug. You can work around it by 1) restricting xi be slightly positive as in<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">real</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.000001</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> xi</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>and\r\n by 2) moving the calculation of the rhos into a generated quantities \r\nblock at the end instead of the transformed parameters block<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">generated quantities </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> upper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rho</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  rho</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_B_raw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sqrt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_B_raw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_B_raw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  rho</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_B_raw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sqrt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_B_raw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_B_raw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  rho</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_B_raw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sqrt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_B_raw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_B_raw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>In\r\n addition, although this is largely unrelated to the bug, if you are \r\ngoing to specify a uniform (0,100) prior on xi, then you should specify \r\nan upper bound on xi&#39;s support, like<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">real</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.000001</span><span style=\"color:#660\">, upper=100&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> xi</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><span style=\"color:#660\"></span></div></code></div><br>in which case, you do not need to explicitly specify the uniform prior on xi in the model block.<br><br>With\r\n all that, your model seems to run, albeit painfully slowly. There is a \r\nlot of new stuff in the Stan manual for v1.1.0 on reparameterizing \r\nmodels like this in Chapter 13.<br><br>Ben<br></div><div><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "doS_gCy7Gw0J",
