   "subject": "Re: [stan-users] Re: stan runtime error \"Exception: boost::too_many_args: format-string referred...\"",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n                <div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:13px\">Thanks Ben and Daniel.<div><br></div><div>The slightly positive lower bound on `xi` did the trick. But I get the same error if I try to specify an upper bound of 100 instead of the uniform prior.</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div></div>\r\n                <div><div><br></div><div>Will Morris M.Phil.</div><div>--- <a href=\"http://wkmor1.wordpress.com\" style=\"color:rgb(0,106,227)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://wkmor1.wordpress.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468625316000&amp;usg=AOvVaw37bRfUVLiW9W1EFQ3gGK2Y\">http://wkmor1.wordpress.com</a></div><div>Publications: <a href=\"http://scholar.google.com.au/citations?user=kgytuo0AAAAJ&amp;hl=en\" style=\"color:rgb(0,106,227);font-size:10pt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://scholar.google.com.au/citations?user%3Dkgytuo0AAAAJ%26hl%3Den&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468625316000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1Q6CEHfqyQ4rtW510YuD4h\">Google Scholar</a></div><div>Twitter: @wkmor1</div><div>Skype: wkmor1</div><div>Phone: <a href=\"tel:+61%203%208344%208086\" value=\"+61383448086\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">+61 3 8344 8086</a></div><div>----------------------------------------------------------------------</div><div>Quantitative and Applied Ecology Group</div><div>--- <a href=\"http://qaeco.com\" style=\"color:rgb(0,106,227)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://qaeco.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468625316000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0ol-hYn2QcaWjTCjMSNlC3\">http://qaeco.com</a></div><div>The School of Botany</div><div>The University of Melbourne</div><div>----------------------------------------------------------------------</div><div>Environmental Decisions Group</div><div>--- <a href=\"http://www.edg.org.au/\" style=\"color:rgb(0,106,227)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.edg.org.au/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468625316000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1OZT1D0Kzt51eUSl2kiIis\">http://www.edg.org.au/</a></div><div>ARC - Centre of Excellence for </div><div>Environmental Decisions</div><div>--- <a href=\"http://ceed.edu.au/\" style=\"color:rgb(0,106,227)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://ceed.edu.au/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468625316000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tpFjilZ8aen4I1_11t_Zc\">http://ceed.edu.au/</a></div><div>NERP Environmental Decisions Hub</div><div>--- <a href=\"http://www.nerpdecisions.edu.au/\" style=\"color:rgb(0,106,227)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.nerpdecisions.edu.au/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468625316000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2ITjn3yFkvnLFwbw4MjS3P\">http://www.nerpdecisions.edu.au/</a></div><div>----------------------------------------------------------------------</div><div>$_$__ ,</div><div> U___ }</div><div>  | |   | |</div><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r\n                 \r\n                <p style=\"color:#a0a0a8\">On Thursday, 20 December 2012 at 8:15 PM, Ben Goodrich wrote:</p>\r\n                "
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<blockquote type=\"cite\" style=\"border-left-style:solid;border-width:1px;margin-left:0px;padding-left:10px\"><span><div><div>On Wednesday, December 19, 2012 10:06:42 PM UTC-5, Will Morris wrote:<br><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>Could someone please help me out with this runtime error (below) I am getting. Have tried to run this model (<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px\"><a href=\"http://cl.ly/131S3n330Z1K\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://cl.ly/131S3n330Z1K&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468625316000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2z_B8QHWAJSnm4H4peBTAg\">http://cl.ly/131S3n330Z1K</a></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px\">, with data </span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px\"><a href=\"http://cl.ly/code/0G3z0o441S0E\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://cl.ly/code/0G3z0o441S0E&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468625316000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0pnOnz_JFE4IiAV0X7Ld3K\">http://cl.ly/code/0G3z0o441S0E</a></span>)\r\n on both a Mac and Linux with optimisation on and off. Both give this  \r\nerror I can&#39;t interpret. Stan (v-1.1.0) itself is working fine as I can  \r\nrun the example models without error.</div></blockquote><div><br>This is our bug. You can work around it by 1) restricting xi be slightly positive as in<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">real</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.000001</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> xi</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>and\r\n by 2) moving the calculation of the rhos into a generated quantities  \r\nblock at the end instead of the transformed parameters block<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">generated quantities </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> upper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rho</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  rho</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_B_raw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sqrt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_B_raw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_B_raw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  rho</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_B_raw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sqrt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_B_raw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_B_raw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  rho</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_B_raw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sqrt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_B_raw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_B_raw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>In\r\n addition, although this is largely unrelated to the bug, if you are  \r\ngoing to specify a uniform (0,100) prior on xi, then you should specify  \r\nan upper bound on xi&#39;s support, like<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">real</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.000001</span><span style=\"color:#660\">, upper=100&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> xi</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><span style=\"color:#660\"></span></div></code></div><br>in which case, you do not need to explicitly specify the uniform prior on xi in the model block.<br><br>With\r\n all that, your model seems to run, albeit painfully slowly. There is a  \r\nlot of new stuff in the Stan manual for v1.1.0 on reparameterizing  \r\nmodels like this in Chapter 13.<br><br>Ben<br></div><div><br></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></div></div></span></blockquote>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<blockquote type=\"cite\" style=\"border-left-style:solid;border-width:1px;margin-left:0px;padding-left:10px\"><span><div><div>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\n <br>\r\n <br>\r\n</div></div></span>\r\n                 \r\n                 \r\n                 \r\n                 \r\n                </blockquote>\r\n                 \r\n                <div>\r\n                    <br>\r\n                </div>\r\n            "
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
