   "subject": "Re: [stan-users] Re: stan runtime error \"Exception: boost::too_many_args: format-string referred...\"",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks for bringing up the issue. That was definitely a bug in Stan. The fix will appear in the next release. (commit 25509af)<div><br></div><div>If you&#39;re willing, try your model with the current source. As of today, the main branch is pretty stable.</div>\r\n<div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Daniel</div><div><br></div><div><div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Thu, Dec 20, 2012 at 7:52 PM, William Morris <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">wkm...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n</div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n                <div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:13px\">Thanks Ben and Daniel.<div><br></div><div>The slightly positive lower bound on `xi` did the trick. But I get the same error if I try to specify an upper bound of 100 instead of the uniform prior.</div>\r\n<div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div></div>\r\n                <div><div><br></div><div>Will Morris M.Phil.</div><div>--- <a href=\"http://wkmor1.wordpress.com\" style=\"color:rgb(0,106,227)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://wkmor1.wordpress.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468625324000&amp;usg=AOvVaw07IyVLUHGMSGk4VqYAUy2k\">http://wkmor1.wordpress.com</a></div><div>Publications: <a href=\"http://scholar.google.com.au/citations?user=kgytuo0AAAAJ&amp;hl=en\" style=\"color:rgb(0,106,227);font-size:10pt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://scholar.google.com.au/citations?user%3Dkgytuo0AAAAJ%26hl%3Den&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468625324000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1BaokTLR9rsC_KKJRC01dG\">Google Scholar</a></div>\r\n<div>Twitter: @wkmor1</div><div>Skype: wkmor1</div><div>Phone: <a href=\"tel:%2B61%203%208344%208086\" value=\"+61383448086\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">+61 3 8344 8086</a></div><div>----------------------------------------------------------------------</div>\r\n<div>Quantitative and Applied Ecology Group</div><div>--- <a href=\"http://qaeco.com\" style=\"color:rgb(0,106,227)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://qaeco.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468625324000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3tXUM6cyDhgJ937AT2IGX-\">http://qaeco.com</a></div><div>The School of Botany</div><div>The University of Melbourne</div>\r\n<div>----------------------------------------------------------------------</div><div>Environmental Decisions Group</div><div>--- <a href=\"http://www.edg.org.au/\" style=\"color:rgb(0,106,227)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.edg.org.au/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468625324000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0vEBqvMsbfd1Xqzq9XR6_B\">http://www.edg.org.au/</a></div>\r\n<div>ARC - Centre of Excellence for </div><div>Environmental Decisions</div><div>--- <a href=\"http://ceed.edu.au/\" style=\"color:rgb(0,106,227)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://ceed.edu.au/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468625324000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2vh_Syky_tZScDFSO3QpE-\">http://ceed.edu.au/</a></div><div>NERP Environmental Decisions Hub</div>\r\n<div>--- <a href=\"http://www.nerpdecisions.edu.au/\" style=\"color:rgb(0,106,227)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.nerpdecisions.edu.au/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468625324000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0UlViuK45tNxr4jzRZbi7U\">http://www.nerpdecisions.edu.au/</a></div><div>----------------------------------------------------------------------</div><div>\r\n$_$__ ,</div><div> U___ }</div><div>  | |   | |</div><div><br></div></div><div><div>\r\n                 \r\n                <p style=\"color:#a0a0a8\">On Thursday, 20 December 2012 at 8:15 PM, Ben Goodrich wrote:</p>\r\n                <blockquote type=\"cite\" style=\"border-left-style:solid;border-width:1px;margin-left:0px;padding-left:10px\">\r\n                    <span><div><div>On Wednesday, December 19, 2012 10:06:42 PM UTC-5, Will Morris wrote:<br><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>Could someone please help me out with this runtime error (below) I am getting. Have tried to run this model (<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px\"><a href=\"http://cl.ly/131S3n330Z1K\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://cl.ly/131S3n330Z1K&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468625324000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3zHrZdNEhcO6RRa2rE68fv\">http://cl.ly/131S3n330Z1K</a></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px\">, with data </span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px\"><a href=\"http://cl.ly/code/0G3z0o441S0E\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://cl.ly/code/0G3z0o441S0E&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468625325000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1hUuz7GXHW0by54uJgrUL1\">http://cl.ly/code/<u></u>0G3z0o441S0E</a></span>)\r\n on both a Mac and Linux with optimisation on and off. Both give this  \r\nerror I can&#39;t interpret. Stan (v-1.1.0) itself is working fine as I can  \r\nrun the example models without error.</div></blockquote><div><br>This is our bug. You can work around it by 1) restricting xi be slightly positive as in<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\">\r\n<code><div><span>real</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span>lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.000001</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span> xi</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span><br>\r\n</span></div></code></div><br>and\r\n by 2) moving the calculation of the rhos into a generated quantities  \r\nblock at the end instead of the transformed parameters block<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span>generated quantities </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span><br>\r\n  real</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span>lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> upper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span> rho</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span><br>\r\n  rho</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_B_raw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span> sqrt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_B_raw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_B_raw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]);</span><span><br>\r\n  rho</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_B_raw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span> sqrt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_B_raw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_B_raw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]);</span><span><br>\r\n  rho</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_B_raw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span> sqrt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_B_raw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_B_raw</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]);</span><span><br>\r\n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span><br></span></div></code></div><br>In\r\n addition, although this is largely unrelated to the bug, if you are  \r\ngoing to specify a uniform (0,100) prior on xi, then you should specify  \r\nan upper bound on xi&#39;s support, like<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\">\r\n<code><div><span>real</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span>lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.000001</span><span style=\"color:#660\">, upper=100&gt;</span><span> xi</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span><br>\r\n</span></div></code></div><span style=\"color:#660\"></span></div></code></div><br>in which case, you do not need to explicitly specify the uniform prior on xi in the model block.<br><br>With\r\n all that, your model seems to run, albeit painfully slowly. There is a  \r\nlot of new stuff in the Stan manual for v1.1.0 on reparameterizing  \r\nmodels like this in Chapter 13.<br><br>Ben<br></div><div><br></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\n <br>\r\n <br>\r\n</div></div></span>\r\n                 \r\n                 \r\n                 \r\n                 \r\n                </blockquote>\r\n                 \r\n                <div>\r\n                    <br>\r\n                </div>\r\n            \r\n\r\n<p></p></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
